      "answer": "It is a condition on a particular use, not a general manufacturing requirement. It applies to occupying an approved child restraint system on board a U.S.-registered civil aircraft during movement on the surface, takeoff, and landing, provided the child is accompanied as specified and the operator complies with required securing/weight conditions; booster-type, vest- and harness-type, and lap held child restraints remain unapproved unless specifically excepted, and the section generally excludes operations under part 121, 125, or 135 and persons subject to § 91.105.",
      "conclusion": "no"
    },
