        }
      ],
      "answer": "No. The restraint system must also meet additional requirements, including being furnished by the operator or an authorized person, having the child accompanied by an authorized adult, not being an unapproved booster, vest/harness, or lap-held restraint (unless excepted), and the operator properly securing the restraint to an approved forward-facing seat/berth, properly securing the child within specified weight limits, and ensuring the system bears the appropriate label(s).",
      "conclusion": "no"
    }
  ]
